  <Patch Id="UjfEplsCqkndux6t5sp2tf">
    <Canvas Id="MTgmpHCsKDglCNIdurVNfi" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="BCbpyFpJ2iD57W2RCKQUN5">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="TElCjmsXGlfhY9UXICGQJT">
        <Canvas Id="UK2Q6v84A228bIU0wWkFc3" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="HvSz66SKy8LuewmzpZc7Ym" Bounds="-820,-120,640,560" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ACT IV LAB - Experiment: two layouts. NOT a shipped unit.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The same 754 features twice on disk. ONE FILE: help/Assets/haneda.geojson, 307,320 bytes.&#xD;&#xA;MANY FILES: lab/Assets/haneda-tiles/, the identical features cut into an 8 x 8 grid by centroid,&#xD;&#xA;32 small files, median about 9 KB.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;MOVE THE MOUSE OVER THE GRID. Both pipelines answer the same question - how many features have&#xD;&#xA;their centre in this cell? - and their IN CELL numbers must always agree, exactly as chapter 11's&#xD;&#xA;two Accepted numbers do. Then read BYTES READ: the one-file answer costs 307,320 bytes and a parse&#xD;&#xA;of all 754 features, every time the question changes. The many-files answer costs one small file -&#xD;&#xA;often thirty times less, sometimes six hundred - because the question's location picked the file.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THAT IS THE WHOLE EXPERIMENT: the data did not change, the answer did not change; only the LAYOUT&#xD;&#xA;changed, and the layout decided how much had to be read. On a local disk both are instant. Over a&#xD;&#xA;network, bytes are latency and money - and this gap is the entire reason cloud-native formats&#xD;&#xA;(GeoParquet's row groups, COG's internal tiling, PMTiles' directory) organise bytes by WHERE.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Honest edges: the split is by centroid, so a feature belongs to exactly one cell - real tilers&#xD;&#xA;clip or duplicate instead, and must say so. An empty cell has NO file: the reader fails, Status&#xD;&#xA;says why, and absence is an answer you can read off the directory itself. The mono side re-reads&#xD;&#xA;per query on purpose - that is what 'ask a fresh question of a remote file' costs; a local cache&#xD;&#xA;would hide exactly the thing being measured.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Rules of the lab: no new library surface, results in docs/ACT-IV-LAB.md. Derived from&#xD;&#xA;help/Assets/haneda.geojson (OpenStreetMap, ODbL - same terms, see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
